Test certificates for x509.rs, each under the name the tests use.

Real chains as the servers sent them on 2026-11-05 (openssl s_client
-showcerts), leaf first, and the anchors they end at, from Mozilla's
set of 2026-10-20. The rest is a test PKI made with openssl 3.6: P-256
unless named otherwise, valid from 2026-01-01 to 2036-01-01.

  root        a CA
  inter       a CA under root
  twin        inter's name, another key
  leaf        under inter: api.example.test, *.wild.example.test,
              192.0.2.1, 2001:db8::1
  leaf384     a P-384 key under inter, signed with SHA-384
  client      under inter, EKU clientAuth only
  crit        under inter, with a critical extension 1.2.3.4
  zero        a CA under root, pathLen 0
  below       a CA under zero
  deep        a leaf under below
  notca       a leaf under inter
  undernotca  a leaf under notca
  cl          a CA under root, EKU clientAuth
  undercl     a leaf under cl
  nc          a CA under root: permitted DNS example.test and IP
              192.0.2.0/24, excluded DNS bad.example.test
  ncgood      under nc: good.example.test, 192.0.2.5
  ncother     under nc: good.example.test, other.test
  ncbad       under nc: x.bad.example.test
  ncstar      under nc: *.example.test
  ncip        under nc: good.example.test, 198.51.100.7
  rsaroot     an RSA-2048 CA
  rsaleaf     an RSA-2048 leaf under it, signed with PSS and SHA-256
  rsapkcs     an RSA-2048 leaf under it, signed with PKCS #1 and SHA-384
  late        a leaf under inter for api.example.test, issued 2026-06-01
  anyroot     a CA
  anyca       a CA under anyroot, EKU anyExtendedKeyUsage only
  underany    a leaf under anyca for api.example.test
  anyleaf     a leaf under anyroot for api.example.test, EKU
              anyExtendedKeyUsage only
  p521root    a P-521 CA, signed with SHA-512
  p521leaf    a P-521 leaf under it for api.example.test, SHA-512
  rsa512root  an RSA-2048 CA, signed with PKCS #1 and SHA-512
  rsa512leaf  an RSA-2048 leaf under it, PSS and SHA-512
  rsa512pkcs  the same key under it, PKCS #1 and SHA-512
  ncmail      a CA under anyroot: critical permitted rfc822Name and URI
              .example.test
  ncmaildns   under ncmail: api.example.test
  ncmailbox   under ncmail: api.example.test, x@example.test
  ncmailuri   under ncmail: api.example.test, https://api.example.test/
  ncmailsub   a CA under ncmail, no subjectAltName, an emailAddress in
              its subject
  ncmailsubleaf  under ncmailsub: api.example.test
  ncdir       a CA under anyroot: critical permitted directoryName
              C=XX, O=rr Test (UTF8String)
  ncdirgood   under ncdir: C=XX, O=rr Test, CN=api.example.test
  ncdirfold   under ncdir: C=xx, O="  RR   TEST ", CN=api.example.test
  ncdirbad    under ncdir: C=XX, O=rr Other, CN=api.example.test
  caleaf      a leaf under anyroot for api.example.test with cA TRUE
  kencleaf    a leaf under anyroot for api.example.test, keyUsage
              keyEncipherment only
  imposedroot a CA, which tests impose name constraints on
  imposedtr   under imposedroot: api.example.tr
  imposedtest under imposedroot: api.example.test
  v1root      a v1 certificate, self-signed
  v1leaf      under v1root: api.example.test
  selfleaf    self-signed for api.example.test, cA FALSE
  underself   under selfleaf: api.example.test
  rsa8192root an RSA-8192 CA, PKCS #1 and SHA-256
  rsa8192leaf under it: api.example.test

The certificates from ncmail on were added on 2026-11-08 under keys of
their own, by the same openssl commands (req and x509 -req, with the
extensions named; v1root by req -x509 -x509v1).

